    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0792" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg668"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/99: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-24T13:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1921—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>141. My despatches 106, 120 and 174.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d637-f1"/> Government
                    has delivered ultimatum to the Costa Rica Oil Corporation demanding immediate
                    reference dispute to sole arbitrator. Oil corporation privately informed
                    President Acosta has announced that he intends to declare forfeiture of
                    corporation and that he has assurance of Department <pb facs="0793" n="669"
                        xml:id="pg669"/> of State that such action will not be opposed. Please refer
                    to penultimate paragraph of your instruction No. 7 December 13, 1920.<anchor
                        n="29" xml:id="d637-f2"/> Is it desired that the Legation take any
                    action?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
